Finding Part 2: For the lowest mode (j = 1), alpha_1 = 0.4903 approx 1/2.
Because a_1 ~ Delta_1^{1/2}, the term a_1^2 / Delta_1 is genuinely finite and O(1) (~ 5.79),
completely harmless in M_1. But in M_2, the squared denominator yields
a_1^2 / Delta_1^2 ~ 1 / Delta_1 ~ 1.33 x 10^40, which accounts for 100.00% of M_2!

