============================================================================================
CELL 60 CONCLUSION: NUMERICAL EVIDENCE FOR A SQUARE-ROOT SPECTRAL OVERLAP LAW
============================================================================================
1. THE EXPONENTIALLY COLLAPSING LOW-ENERGY TOWER:
   The Galerkin matrix exhibits an exponentially collapsing low-energy tower in both
   parity sectors: E_0 ~ 10^-43, mu_odd,1 ~ 10^-40, E_even,1 ~ 10^-37, mu_odd,2 ~ 10^-34.
   The operator norm of the odd resolvent is indeed catastrophically large (~ 10^39).

2. THE SQUARE-ROOT OVERLAP PHENOMENON:
   The lowest odd-sector overlap satisfies numerically:
       |a_1| / sqrt(Delta_1) = O(1),
   with the observed values remaining near 2 across the tested dimensions (1.97 to 2.76).
   Consequently:
       a_1^2 / Delta_1 = O(1) (~ 5.79),      a_1^2 / Delta_1^2 = O(Delta_1^-1) (~ 1.33e+40),
   explaining the simultaneous boundedness of M_1 and the astronomical value of M_2.

3. THE EXACT COMMUTATOR CONNECTION:
   The exact commutator identity [Q, K] = -psi d^T + d psi^T projected onto <e_1, . c>
   yields the exact relationship:
       Delta_1 <e_1, K c> = -D_0 a_1   ==>   a_1 = - (Delta_1 / D_0) <e_1, K c>.
   The numerical data suggest the common scaling D_0^2 asymp Delta_1 and <e_1, K c> = O(1),
   which would naturally enforce the square-root overlap law |a_1| ~ sqrt(Delta_1).

4. RESOLUTION IN THE EXCITED EVEN SECTOR:
   In the even sector, the source overlap b_k = <u_k, s_2> is small enough that the quotient
   tau_k = (d_k b_k) / Delta_k remains finite (tau_k ~ 10^3 - 10^4), summing to D_1/D_0 ~ 5.2e+5.
